Additional Use Grant

Subject to the terms and conditions of this License, the Licensor hereby grants
you the right to use, copy, modify, and redistribute the Licensed Work,
provided that all of the following conditions are met.

These conditions mirror the product charter that is encoded in the Licensed
Work itself, in `apps/desktop/electron/cakal-identity.cjs` (the `IMMUTABLE_CORE`
list, referred to as the "ürün anayasası" / product constitution). The charter
is enforced mechanically by the preflight gate and the protected-paths
mechanism; these license conditions bind the same limits contractually, so that
removing the mechanism does not remove the obligation.

1. **Project Name and Identity:** The name "ÇAKAL" (or "CAKAL") must not be
   removed or replaced when distributing or deploying a modified version of the
   Licensed Work. Any modified version must clearly state that it is a
   derivative of ÇAKAL and must not misrepresent itself as the original work.

2. **Core Purpose:** The core purpose of the Licensed Work — a personal,
   single-user AI-powered research and opportunity assistant that researches,
   analyses and advises — must not be changed. In particular it must not be
   turned into a multi-tenant SaaS product, a general-purpose autonomous
   operator, or an automated trading system.

3. **No Execution on Real Assets:** The Licensed Work must not be given the
   ability to execute transactions on real money, securities, crypto assets or
   financial accounts, nor to place, modify or cancel orders or transfers. This
   condition is absolute: per-action user confirmation does not lift it. More
   generally, the Licensed Work must not be extended to perform actions on the
   user's behalf whose consequences are hard to reverse, public, financial or
   legal in nature.

4. **Evidence Discipline:** The deterministic decision locks (`decision-guards.cjs`,
   "karar kilidi") that prevent AL/SAT (BUY/SELL) verdicts without sufficient
   fresh evidence must not be removed or weakened. Financial assessments must
   continue to carry source, evidence and confidence; where data is insufficient,
   the Licensed Work must continue to withhold a definite verdict rather than
   produce one.

5. **Security and Permission Gates:** The following must not be removed,
   disabled or circumvented in any distributed or deployed version: the
   `surgery/` directory and its `protected-paths` mechanism; the two-layer
   permission gate (hard-block layer + user-confirmation layer) that governs
   source-code modifications; the sandbox plugin runner; the Secret Broker; the
   preflight gate; and the safe-path and command guards. The Licensed Work must
   not be enabled to modify its own source code directly, and any coding agent
   used for maintenance must remain a temporary surgeon rather than becoming a
   persistent agent or a second identity.

6. **Audit Integrity:** Audit and activity records must not be deleted, hidden
   or rendered unverifiable.

